# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# FABOM GLOBAL — environment variables
# Copy this file to `.env.local` for local development, or add the values in
# your Vercel project dashboard (Settings → Environment Variables).
# NEVER commit real keys to version control.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Contact form → email delivery (RECOMMENDED) ─────────────────────────────
# Create a FREE access key in 2 minutes:
#   1. Go to https://web3forms.com
#   2. Enter emmanuelfabom121@gmail.com and click "Create Access Key"
#   3. Check your Gmail inbox for the confirmation email from Web3Forms
#      and click the access key link they send you
#   4. Paste the key below / into Vercel
# From then on, every form submission arrives directly in that Gmail inbox.
WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY=""

# ── Alternative email provider (optional) ────────────────────────────────────
# If you prefer Resend (https://resend.com), create an API key and set it
# here instead of Web3Forms. Full instructions: README.md → "Email delivery".
RESEND_API_KEY=""

# Where enquiries are delivered when using Resend
# (defaults to the business email when empty; ignored by Web3Forms, which
# always delivers to the address tied to your access key).
CONTACT_TO_EMAIL=""

# The "from" address on enquiry emails sent through Resend.
# Without a verified domain, leave the default onboarding sender.
CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL=""

# ── Public site URL (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Used for SEO metadata, the sitemap and robots.txt. Set it to the live
# address after deploying, e.g. https://fabomglobal.vercel.app
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=""

# ── Database (OPTIONAL backup copy of enquiries) ─────────────────────────────
# The contact form works WITHOUT a database — enquiries are delivered by
# email. To also keep a copy in a database, point this to a SQLite file
# locally (or a hosted database in production). Leave empty on Vercel.
# DATABASE_URL="file:./db/custom.db"
